<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ extra social spending linked to parental code.</title>
<headline>NZ extra social spending linked to parental code.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New Zealand centre-right coalition government on Thursday outlined extra spending of $900 million in the 1997/98 fiscal year mainly on health, education and social welfare, linked to a code of social responsibility which would put obligations on parents receiving state help.</p>
<p>&quot;We will introduce reasonable processes to ensure that we New Zealanders meet these obligations,&quot; Treasurer Winston Peters said in his budget speech.</p>
</text>
